  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a direct relationship between Npc126240 and SMMC-7721, mediated through Microtubule-associated protein 1B. This protein is identified as a target of Npc126240, and in turn, it is a target of multiple compounds, including 5-Oxobrucine and a complex organic molecule. All these targets ultimately lead to SMMC-7721, indicating a hierarchical pathway where Npc126240 exerts its effect through the modulation of Microtubule-associated protein 1B, which in turn influences the cell line SMMC-7721. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust and reliable connection, with the mechanism likely involving the regulation of microtubule dynamics or cellular processes that are critical for the survival or function of SMMC-7721. The evidence supports a clear, albeit indirect, link between Npc126240 and SMMC-7721, emphasizing the role of Microtubule-associated protein 1B as a central mediator in this relationship.",
